1
00:00:06,300 --> 00:00:07,679
Last time, we asked:

2
00:00:07,699 --> 00:00:08,749
A caterpillar!

3
00:00:09,049 --> 00:00:11,279
One day, it will become a butterfly.

4
00:00:11,559 --> 00:00:14,649
Is the caterpillar a nymph, like the young grasshopper?

5
00:00:14,695 --> 00:00:15,805
One, yes.

6
00:00:17,025 --> 00:00:17,905
Two, no.

7
00:00:19,383 --> 00:00:20,893
Hold on to your answer!

8
00:00:22,765 --> 00:00:25,095
A little moth is hiding in this video.

9
00:00:25,345 --> 00:00:26,585
Can you spot it?

10
00:00:26,709 --> 00:00:28,359
Moths rest in the daytime.

11
00:00:28,459 --> 00:00:30,449
Look on the walls, and under the leaves!

12
00:00:30,499 --> 00:00:31,959
You against the Buddies!

13
00:00:32,229 --> 00:00:34,079
Lock in first with your fingers.

14
00:00:34,349 --> 00:00:36,179
One finger for every point.

15
00:00:36,760 --> 00:00:38,090
Today you'll learn:

16
00:00:38,286 --> 00:00:40,166
The 4-stage life cycle.

17
00:00:40,365 --> 00:00:41,875
Larva and pupa.

18
00:00:42,127 --> 00:00:43,345
What prolegs are.

19
00:00:43,939 --> 00:00:44,879
Are you ready?

20
00:00:45,319 --> 00:00:46,089
Three!

21
00:00:46,469 --> 00:00:47,129
Two!

22
00:00:47,499 --> 00:00:48,149
One!

23
00:00:48,569 --> 00:00:49,289
Go!

24
00:00:50,678 --> 00:00:51,568
Round one!

25
00:00:51,878 --> 00:00:53,508
Is the caterpillar a nymph?

26
00:00:53,798 --> 00:00:55,108
Show me your fingers!

27
00:00:58,576 --> 00:00:59,556
Locked in!

28
00:00:59,684 --> 00:01:04,024
One! It is a young insect that munches leaves, just like the grasshopper

29
00:01:04,044 --> 00:01:04,684
nymph.

30
00:01:04,924 --> 00:01:06,274
So it must be a nymph!

31
00:01:06,321 --> 00:01:09,511
Two. A nymph looks like a small adult.

32
00:01:09,711 --> 00:01:12,821
But this caterpillar looks nothing like a butterfly.

33
00:01:12,923 --> 00:01:15,019
Two! A butterfly has big wings.

34
00:01:15,039 --> 00:01:18,851
This caterpillar is just a long, green tube that eats!

35
00:01:19,160 --> 00:01:21,790
The answer is two: no, it is not a nymph!

36
00:01:22,070 --> 00:01:23,100
Two fingers?

37
00:01:23,370 --> 00:01:24,580
One finger up!

38
00:01:24,707 --> 00:01:26,007
Then what is it?

39
00:01:26,027 --> 00:01:28,197
It is long and soft, and it wriggles.

40
00:01:28,237 --> 00:01:29,437
Is it a worm?

41
00:01:30,086 --> 00:01:31,236
Look closer.

42
00:01:31,826 --> 00:01:33,556
Count the legs at the front.

43
00:01:34,126 --> 00:01:36,179
Then look at the little stumps at the back.

44
00:01:36,199 --> 00:01:39,319
One, two, three pairs of pointed legs at the front.

45
00:01:39,409 --> 00:01:41,931
That is six legs, so it is an insect!

46
00:01:41,951 --> 00:01:45,131
Like all insects, caterpillars have six legs.

47
00:01:45,718 --> 00:01:48,478
The stumps at the back are not real legs.

48
00:01:49,048 --> 00:01:50,808
They are called prolegs.

49
00:01:51,868 --> 00:01:54,258
Prolegs are pretend legs with tiny hooks.

50
00:01:54,278 --> 00:01:57,048
The hooks grip the twig, so the caterpillar can hold on and

51
00:01:57,068 --> 00:01:58,158
crawl along!

52
00:02:00,863 --> 00:02:02,013
Say it with me!

53
00:02:02,727 --> 00:02:05,987
Prolegs are false legs that help the caterpillars to move.

54
00:02:08,760 --> 00:02:10,150
Be a butterfly egg!

55
00:02:10,460 --> 00:02:11,450
Shrink down.

56
00:02:11,730 --> 00:02:12,660
Quietly.

57
00:02:14,947 --> 00:02:17,967
You are a tiny round egg, stuck on a lime leaf.

58
00:02:18,747 --> 00:02:20,757
Days go by, and you hatch.

59
00:02:21,537 --> 00:02:23,187
You are a little caterpillar!

60
00:02:23,698 --> 00:02:26,038
You munch the leaf, and munch, and munch.

61
00:02:26,818 --> 00:02:30,178
Your skin gets tight, so you moult, and you grow bigger.

62
00:02:30,692 --> 00:02:32,462
One day, you stop eating.

63
00:02:33,262 --> 00:02:35,122
You hang very still from a stem.

64
00:02:35,641 --> 00:02:37,821
Your skin splits one last time.

65
00:02:38,621 --> 00:02:40,711
Underneath, there is a hard case.

66
00:02:41,501 --> 00:02:42,731
You are a pupa!

67
00:02:44,455 --> 00:02:47,875
The butterfly larva is also called a caterpillar.

68
00:02:48,386 --> 00:02:51,016
So the caterpillar is the butterfly's larva.

69
00:02:51,136 --> 00:02:54,506
A larva is the young, and it looks nothing like the adult!

70
00:02:54,557 --> 00:02:58,227
The larva eats a lot and moults many times as it grows.

71
00:02:58,963 --> 00:03:01,463
Now it does not move, and it does not eat.

72
00:03:01,613 --> 00:03:03,333
So nothing is happening in there.

73
00:03:03,353 --> 00:03:05,473
It is just resting!

74
00:03:05,602 --> 00:03:07,162
Something is not right.

75
00:03:07,432 --> 00:03:09,612
If you can spot it, cross your arms.

76
00:03:09,892 --> 00:03:10,852
Hold on!

77
00:03:16,265 --> 00:03:17,395
Arms crossed?

78
00:03:17,665 --> 00:03:18,875
One finger up!

79
00:03:18,927 --> 00:03:21,507
It does not eat, but it is alive and very busy.

80
00:03:21,747 --> 00:03:24,797
Inside its case, it is changing into a butterfly!

81
00:03:24,927 --> 00:03:26,967
This stage is called the pupa.

82
00:03:29,057 --> 00:03:30,207
Look closer.

83
00:03:30,837 --> 00:03:33,617
On the outside, the pupa hardly moves.

84
00:03:34,167 --> 00:03:37,457
But inside the pupal case, the body is changing.

85
00:03:37,515 --> 00:03:38,825
It does not eat.

86
00:03:39,385 --> 00:03:43,185
It continues to develop into an adult in the pupal case.

87
00:03:43,697 --> 00:03:46,627
So the pupa is busy, like a cake in the oven.

88
00:03:46,737 --> 00:03:49,997
You cannot see it change, but it is changing inside!

89
00:03:51,178 --> 00:03:55,588
Then the pupal case splits, and out comes the adult: a butterfly!

90
00:03:56,498 --> 00:03:59,888
Its wings are all crumpled, like my bedsheet in the morning.

91
00:04:00,128 --> 00:04:01,798
Now they are spreading out flat!

92
00:04:04,778 --> 00:04:07,948
The butterfly has four stages in its life cycle.

93
00:04:08,208 --> 00:04:12,078
The stages are the egg, the larva, the pupa and the adult.

94
00:04:13,692 --> 00:04:14,982
Say it with me!

95
00:04:15,688 --> 00:04:18,818
Some animals have four stages in their life cycles.

96
00:04:19,298 --> 00:04:22,348
The young of these animals do not look like the adult.

97
00:04:24,824 --> 00:04:26,294
Show me your score hand!

98
00:04:26,564 --> 00:04:27,884
More than one finger?

99
00:04:28,204 --> 00:04:29,564
You beat the Buddies.

100
00:04:29,844 --> 00:04:30,874
Two fingers?

101
00:04:31,144 --> 00:04:32,154
High five!

102
00:04:32,732 --> 00:04:34,182
Did you spot the moth?

103
00:04:34,432 --> 00:04:36,822
It was on the side of the lime plant's pot!

104
00:04:36,959 --> 00:04:38,549
Here is a fun fact!

105
00:04:38,729 --> 00:04:42,729
Many moth caterpillars spin a silk cocoon, and become a pupa inside

106
00:04:42,749 --> 00:04:46,469
it. The silk for silk clothes comes from a moth's cocoon!

107
00:04:46,591 --> 00:04:47,871
Tell someone at home!

108
00:04:48,600 --> 00:04:50,800
Let's read today's key words together!

109
00:04:51,090 --> 00:04:51,850
Ready?

110
00:04:52,187 --> 00:04:52,940
Prolegs.

111
00:04:54,472 --> 00:04:55,132
Larva.

112
00:04:56,632 --> 00:04:57,432
Pupa.

113
00:04:58,809 --> 00:04:59,749
Well done!

114
00:05:00,546 --> 00:05:02,476
Look in this old pail of rainwater!

115
00:05:02,656 --> 00:05:04,606
Tiny things are wriggling up and down.

116
00:05:04,816 --> 00:05:05,737
What are they?

117
00:05:05,757 --> 00:05:07,347
Find out in Part Two!

118
00:05:08,507 --> 00:05:09,608
Say it with us!

119
00:05:10,408 --> 00:05:11,158
Ready?

120
00:05:11,282 --> 00:05:11,942
One!

121
00:05:12,282 --> 00:05:12,982
two!

122
00:05:13,287 --> 00:05:14,462
Now you know!
